Description: FlickOS security kit: network analysis
 Nmap, Wireshark and tshark, tcpdump, arp-scan, Ettercap and bettercap from
 Debian, with the everyday tools for networks: ncat, socat, dig, whois,
 traceroute, mtr, iperf3, ngrep, tcpflow, and the SMB, LDAP, NetBIOS and
 SNMP clients.
 .
 Capturing packets needs administrator rights as Debian installs it:
 Wireshark lists no interfaces until your account may capture (sudo
 dpkg-reconfigure wireshark-common, add yourself to the wireshark group and
 log in again). Raw scans stay sudo nmap.
 .
 Use these tools only on computers and networks you own or have permission
 to test.
 .
 A kit is installed from Software's Security Tools and removed there too.
 Nothing it installs runs until it is used
 (docs/design/flickos-security.md).
